-- function values in C. After lifting, a function value is a definition applied to fewer
-- arguments than it takes: a block [the definition's wrapper][its arity][how many are held][the
-- held arguments]. hy_app gives one more argument: with the last one the wrapper is called on all
-- of them, before that a block holding one more is made
